---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Carousel from "../components/Carousel.astro";

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

<Layout>
  <header class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">St. Petersburg Citywide Referendum | November 3, 2026</p>
        <h1>Harborage Marina Lease Extension Referendum</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          A proposed new 30-year lease term would support approximately $2.15
          million in planned improvements to a nearly 40-year-old marina while
          the submerged lands remain City-owned.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-buttons">
          <a
            class="btn"
            href="/harborage-marina-presentation.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
          >
            Explore the Proposal
          </a>
          <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="#ballot">Read the Ballot Language</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="hero-cta">
        <h2>Ballot Question 2</h2>
        <p class="hero-cta-lead">Vote</p>
        <span class="ballot-option"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>YES</span>
        <ul class="hero-cta-points">
          <li>No cost to taxpayers</li>
          <li>Good for St. Pete</li>
          <li>Good for the future</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <div class="quick-facts">
    <div class="container">
      <ul>
        <li>30-year lease term</li>
        <li>Approximately $2.15 million planned investment</li>
        <li>Required improvements at no cost to the City</li>
        <li>City-owned submerged lands remain City-owned</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section id="proposal">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The Proposal</h2>
      <h3>What voters are deciding</h3>
      <p>
        St. Petersburg voters will decide whether City Council may approve an
        amendment establishing a new 30-year term for the lease of City-owned
        submerged lands at Harborage Marina. The amendment would require
        Harborage Marina to construct 200 linear feet of docks, boat lifts, and
        expanded restrooms at no cost to the City, with the improvements owned
        by the City at the end of the lease. The proposed amendment does not
        expand the existing submerged-land lease boundaries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Approximately $2.15 Million in Planned Improvements</h2>
      <p>
        Harborage Marina states that a new 30-year term would make approximately
        $2.15 million in planned investment financially feasible. Its April 2026
        presentation identifies:
      </p>

      <ul class="costs">
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">Approximately $1 Million</span>
          <span class="cost-title">New Dock</span>
          200 linear feet of new dock with fire suppression, water, and
          electrical service.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">Approximately $650,000</span>
          <span class="cost-title">Boat Lifts</span>
          Boat lifts intended to accommodate additional boaters and larger
          vessels.
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="cost-amount">Approximately $500,000</span>
          <span class="cost-title">Expanded Restrooms</span>
          Expanded restroom facilities.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="note" style="margin-top:1.5rem;">
        The $2.15 million figure is Harborage Marina's estimated investment. The
        ballot requires the specified improvements but does not establish a
        $2.15 million minimum expenditure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <Carousel />

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Harborage Marina and the City</h2>
      <p>
        The marina's lease relationship with the City dates to 1986. According
        to Harborage Marina's April 2026 presentation, its FY2025 annual lease
        contribution to the City was approximately $671,000.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="ballot">
    <div class="container">
      <details class="accordion">
        <summary>
          <span class="accordion-title">Official Ballot Language</span>
          <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <h3 class="ballot-subhead">City of St. Petersburg No. 2 Referendum Question</h3>
          <div class="ballot">
            <h3>
              &ldquo;Authorizing Amendment of Harborage Marina Lease to Extend
              Term to 30 Years and Require Improvements&rdquo;
            </h3>
            <p>
              &ldquo;May City Council approve amendment of the lease of
              City-owned submerged lands at Harborage Marina subject to
              conditions in ordinance 640-H? Such amendment would extend the
              term of the lease to 30 years and require the tenant to construct
              new improvements at no cost to the City, including 200 linear feet
              of docks, boat lifts, and expanded restrooms. Those improvements
              would be owned by the City at the end of the lease.&rdquo;
            </p>
            <div class="ballot-options">
              <span class="ballot-option"><span class="check" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>YES</span>
              <span class="ballot-option ballot-option--no">NO</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Voting Information</h2>
      <p class="voting-lead">November 3, 2026 General Election</p>
      <div class="voting-grid">
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Voter Registration Deadline</span>
          October 5, 2026
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Early Voting</span>
          October 19 through November 1, 2026<br />7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m. daily
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Vote-by-Mail Request Deadline</span>
          October 22, 2026 at 5:00 p.m.
        </div>
        <div class="voting-item">
          <span class="label">Election Day</span>
          Tuesday, November 3, 2026<br />7:00 a.m. to 7:00 p.m.
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.75rem;">
        <a class="btn" href="https://www.votepinellas.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          >View Official Election Information</a
        >
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section>
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary>
          <span class="accordion-title">Who owns the submerged lands?</span>
          <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <p>
            The City of St. Petersburg. The referendum concerns an amendment to
            the lease of City-owned submerged lands.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary>
          <span class="accordion-title">Who pays for the required improvements?</span>
          <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <p>
            The ballot requires Harborage Marina, as the tenant, to construct
            the specified improvements at no cost to the City.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary>
          <span class="accordion-title">
            What happens to the improvements at the end of the lease?
          </span>
          <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <p>
            The ballot states that the improvements would be owned by the City
            at the end of the lease.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>

      <details class="accordion">
        <summary>
          <span class="accordion-title">
            What happens if voters approve the referendum?
          </span>
          <span class="accordion-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <p>
            Approval would authorize City Council to approve the lease amendment
            subject to Ordinance 640-H. Voter approval would not itself execute
            the lease.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <footer>
    <div class="container">
      <p><a href="https://harboragereferendum2026.com">harboragereferendum2026.com</a></p>
      <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:info@harboragereferendum2026.com">info@harboragereferendum2026.com</a></p>
      <p class="note">
        [Insert the exact political advertisement disclaimer approved by
        Harborage's designated compliance contact.]
      </p>
      <p class="note">&copy; {year} Harborage Referendum 2026. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>
</Layout>
